{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00156",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.79,
      "end_seconds": 5.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Okay, doctor, we're all set in here. I'll give you the numbers when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.12,
      "end_seconds": 11.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Welcome, tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.47,
      "end_seconds": 17.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "It's a fever, mostly. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.69,
      "end_seconds": 19.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.4,
      "end_seconds": 32.76,
      "duration_seconds": 10.36,
      "text": "Okay, so probably three days. Yeah. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.35,
      "end_seconds": 37.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.06,
      "end_seconds": 54.76,
      "duration_seconds": 16.7,
      "text": "Honestly, a couple of times a week. It's severe, honestly. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. So, I've also had a blocked nose, for five days. Oh, um, and a mild headache."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.91,
      "end_seconds": 58.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "What's the pattern, is it there all day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.28,
      "end_seconds": 61.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "I'd say every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.57,
      "end_seconds": 66.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "What about a sore throat, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.17,
      "end_seconds": 72.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Yes, actually. Okay, so about sore throat, pretty severe, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.61,
      "end_seconds": 77.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any diarrhoea or stiff neck?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.3,
      "end_seconds": 80.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Well, no, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.55,
      "end_seconds": 84.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Any vomiting, rash or chest pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.77,
      "end_seconds": 88.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Um, no, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.89,
      "end_seconds": 92.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.4,
      "end_seconds": 96.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Okay, so no, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 97.42,
      "end_seconds": 104.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. SpO2 97 percent on room air, pressure 106 over 78, pulse is 108 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.3,
      "end_seconds": 109.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Thanks. Alright, what medicines do you take regularly? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.1,
      "end_seconds": 115.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "It's, It's Asthalin inhaler, when needed for my asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.18,
      "end_seconds": 119.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.23,
      "end_seconds": 124.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, my uncle had colon cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.31,
      "end_seconds": 130.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.58,
      "end_seconds": 138.4,
      "duration_seconds": 7.82,
      "text": "I've had asthma for about a year now. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.49,
      "end_seconds": 140.19,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Mm-hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.22,
      "end_seconds": 145.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.98,
      "end_seconds": 149.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.8,
      "end_seconds": 162.75,
      "duration_seconds": 12.95,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.81,
      "end_seconds": 168.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.43,
      "end_seconds": 174.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "Oh, um, just my tonsils out, when I was a child."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.94,
      "end_seconds": 181.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.75,
      "end_seconds": 193.27,
      "duration_seconds": 10.52,
      "text": "I mean, um, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.02,
      "end_seconds": 198.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.15,
      "end_seconds": 202.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Hold your arm out like this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.44,
      "end_seconds": 220.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Chest is clear when I listen, no crackles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.0,
      "end_seconds": 222.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Open wide for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.76,
      "end_seconds": 245.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "Your throat looks red at the back, but there's no pus on the tonsils."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.35,
      "end_seconds": 261.92,
      "duration_seconds": 11.57,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.0,
      "end_seconds": 278.46,
      "duration_seconds": 15.46,
      "text": "Hmm, for the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.85,
      "end_seconds": 290.53,
      "duration_seconds": 11.68,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, it fits best with a viral illness. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I'd also keep dengue fever in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.77,
      "end_seconds": 296.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Yeah, I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.33,
      "end_seconds": 310.52,
      "duration_seconds": 13.19,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a viral illness is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a fever for three days, severe, and no diarrhoea or rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 310.89,
      "end_seconds": 312.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.99,
      "end_seconds": 321.61,
      "duration_seconds": 8.62,
      "text": "I'm going to order a throat swab, for sore throat. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.78,
      "end_seconds": 325.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.17,
      "end_seconds": 338.48,
      "duration_seconds": 8.31,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange blood tests for fever. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 339.86,
      "end_seconds": 342.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Okay, you know, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 343.61,
      "end_seconds": 348.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Doctor, I did a flu swab before they came in, the result's on your screen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.06,
      "end_seconds": 378.18,
      "duration_seconds": 27.12,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Let's use cetirizine, 10 milligrams, at night, for five days. You take it by mouth. That's for blocked nose. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. I'm prescribing paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed, for three days. That should help with fever and body aches. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.72,
      "end_seconds": 380.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.59,
      "end_seconds": 392.79,
      "duration_seconds": 11.2,
      "text": "Stay home, rest, and keep the fluids up. Warm soups and water, anything that goes down easily. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.18,
      "end_seconds": 400.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.36,
      "text": "Mm-hm. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 401.38,
      "end_seconds": 404.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.05,
      "end_seconds": 409.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Let's review you if it's not settling in three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 410.29,
      "end_seconds": 412.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 413.66,
      "end_seconds": 417.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Wonderful, I think that's it. Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 418.19,
      "end_seconds": 421.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Alright, um, thanks. Bye for now."
    }
  ]
}